From 8e00e5402b0ab95b6121e4559549802b3d5975b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SriAkhilSJ <206201543+SriAkhilSJ@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 15:48:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] docs(runbook): document the scoped emitter, and point 6.5 at
 it
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The chip's STALE cell said "rebuild (§5)" — a 30-minute answer for a seconds-long job. The
contrib bundle under out/ is regenerated by scripts/emit-crusorai-bundle.mjs (scoped to the
crusorai subtree, needs node_modules), which is also what moves SOURCES_HASH. Documented in §5
with the pass condition, and out/ is committed, so a current bundle belongs in the commit.

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 CRUSOR_PREVIEW_DESKTOP_APP_TEST.md | 18 +++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/CRUSOR_PREVIEW_DESKTOP_APP_TEST.md b/CRUSOR_PREVIEW_DESKTOP_APP_TEST.md
index 268a6fa9..7043626e 100644
--- a/CRUSOR_PREVIEW_DESKTOP_APP_TEST.md
+++ b/CRUSOR_PREVIEW_DESKTOP_APP_TEST.md
@@ -152,6 +152,22 @@ npm run gulp minify-vscode
 `minify-vscode` is only needed for a packaged build; for the in-app test `compile` is enough, and
 `scripts\code.bat` will fetch Electron on first launch.
 
+The shipped panel under `desktop\vscode\out\` — 41 tracked files: the crusorai contrib bundle,
+`SOURCES_HASH`, `BUILD_INFO.json` — is regenerated by the scoped emitter. It takes seconds rather than
+a full compile, and it needs `desktop\vscode\node_modules` to exist:
+
+```powershell
+cd D:\pulseAIagent\PulseAIRepo\desktop\vscode
+node scripts\emit-crusorai-bundle.mjs
+```
+
+Run it after any change to the crusorai subtree (a rebuilt `out\` is what makes the chip read current
+instead of `STALE`), and note that `out\` is **committed**, so a current bundle belongs in the commit:
+
+```powershell
+.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest src/tests/test_desktop_renderer_architecture.py::test_engine_hash_matches_the_shipped_panel_on_this_repo -q
+```
+
 If a layer check fails on `crusorai`, send the two lines it prints — that lane is exactly what a
 `browser/` file reaching for a `node/` or electron import would trip, and the preview service is
 `browser/`.
@@ -184,7 +200,7 @@ Then, in the window:
 | 6.2 | Send any prompt, e.g. `hi` | a reply appears, instantly (or after `CRUSORAI_ECHO_DELAY_MS`), and `Stop` is offered while it runs | the engine never started: read the pane's error line. `CrusorAI engine root is not configured: set crusorai.engineRoot or CRUSORAI_ENGINE_ROOT, or open a workspace that contains src/bridge.` means the opened folder is not the checkout and no setting points at it |
 | 6.3 | Confirm which python it used | `PulseAIRepo\.venv\Scripts\python.exe` if it exists, else `CRUSORAI_PYTHON_PATH`, else `python` on PATH | if your `.venv` is elsewhere, set `CRUSORAI_PYTHON_PATH` before launching |
 | 6.4 | Send a second prompt while the first is still running (needs 6.2 with the delay) | the turn queues or refuses cleanly — no silent drop | a silent drop is a real finding: send me the pane text |
-| 6.5 | Look at the engine chip at the bottom of the pane | it reads `ui 2026-09-26` and there is no `STALE` next to it | `STALE` means the `out/` you launched is older than this UI round: rebuild (§5) and relaunch. The stamp bumps with every workbench UI round (`CRUSORAI_UI_STAMP` in `crusorAIRenderer.ts`) |
+| 6.5 | Look at the engine chip at the bottom of the pane | it reads `ui 2026-09-26` and there is no `STALE` next to it | `STALE` means the `out/` you launched is older than this UI round: re-run the emitter (§5), then relaunch. The stamp bumps with every workbench UI round (`CRUSORAI_UI_STAMP` in `crusorAIRenderer.ts`) |
 | 6.6 | The provider-free pass is done | now do a **real** turn: §7 below. It costs money and needs a key, which is why it is a separate section rather than an extra row here | — |
 
 The agent's reply arriving in the app is the whole point of this gate: it proves the workbench →
